## STEP 5: WRITE FINAL ANSWER
```bash
echo "VALUE" > /app/answer.txt
```
- No commas, no dollar signs, no unit labels. Negative: minus sign.
- Percentages: number without % sign.
- Units: same as table unless question says otherwise. If table says "in millions" but question asks "nominal dollars", multiply by 1000000.
- **Multi-value:** If question asks for multiple values (e.g. slope AND intercept), include ALL of them.
  ALWAYS brackets with SPACE after comma: `echo "[val1, val2]" > /app/answer.txt`
  NEVER `[val1,val2]` (no space) — grader will merge numbers into garbage.
- Round only if question specifies rounding. Otherwise give full precision.

## REFERENCE
- FY: pre-1977 = Jul-Jun, post-1976 = Oct-Sep. TQ = Jul-Sep 1976.
- CY: Jan-Dec.
- Population stdev (pstdev) unless question says "sample".
- After computing, ALWAYS overwrite /app/answer.txt with your final number.

